            "summary": "Shares of RV manufacturer Thor Industries (NYSE:THO) fell 6.9% in the afternoon session after its strong third-quarter results were overshadowed by a weak full-year forecast. The company posted earnings per share of 41 cents, significantly beating analyst forecasts of a loss, while sales grew 11.5% year on year to $2.39 billion. Although the stock initially traded higher on the positive results, it reversed course. The drop appeared to be linked to the company's forward-looking guidance. THOR In",
